WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:07.130
The Lenovo IdeaPad S940 is a fantastic looking
windows laptop, honestly one of the best.

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:10.710
The display is very nice, and the keyboard
is a joy to type on.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:16.339
With that said, for the asking price, would
suggest looking elsewhere, and there are a

00:00:16.339 --> 00:00:23.880
few things that disappointed us, but with
that said there is one specific group that

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:30.229
this machine will be fantastic for, and also
a way you can get some solid discounts that

00:00:30.229 --> 00:00:31.999
make this 14” laptop a lot more desirable.

00:00:31.999 --> 00:00:36.011
It’s obvious that we are Mac fans around
here, and coming from that background I have

00:00:36.011 --> 00:00:37.730
to say I love the design.

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:40.989
It’s very MacBook without copying the design.

00:00:40.989 --> 00:00:44.239
In fact, many will even prefer it.

00:00:44.239 --> 00:00:53.920
I love how the back and front slope forward,
the minimally beveled edges, the Lenovo badging

00:00:53.920 --> 00:01:04.949
on the lower right hand side of both the lid
and the inside, along with slightly curved

00:01:04.949 --> 00:01:12.220
and shaped display display bezels presenting
a flat center on the lid for easy opening

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:15.299
with 9 series elegantly embossed.

00:01:15.299 --> 00:01:19.610
The unibody aluminum chassis feels great in
the hand but has a bit too much flex for our

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:24.590
liking, and the overall build quality is below
Apples with some mis-aligned panels.

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:29.300
The touchpad is a decent size with very good
almost uniform clicking but cursor control

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:30.830
is below average.

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:34.650
At the top right we have a slim power button
with led indicator which doesn’t include

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:39.649
a fingerprint scanner but that's totally fine
by us since the s940 offers windows hello

00:01:39.649 --> 00:01:41.659
facial unlocking that we absolutely love.

00:01:41.659 --> 00:01:49.450
Below the 720P HD Webcam and IR sensor our
model has a gorgeous not touch 500 nit 100%

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:56.500
SRGB 4K display capable of HDR playback, but
there is a 400 Nit 1080P option that will

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:59.590
help with battery life, but more on the battery
in just a bit.

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:04.509
The quad speakers are user facing with Dolby
tuning and sound above average for ultra light

00:02:04.509 --> 00:02:10.500
windows laptop, a surprising 2.6 pounds in
this case, but can’t keep up with Apple’s

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:27.880
$1100 Macbook Air or similarly priced 13”
Macbook Pro.

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:32.860
At the center of the laptop is probably the
best feature of this laptop, the backlit keyboard.

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:37.930
The key travel is just long enough to feel
great but still stay thin, with enough pressure

00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:44.300
required to eliminate mis types without feeling
too clicky or damping without being too mushy.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:49.250
If you type a lot this is one of the best
keyboards in any laptop this thin and light.

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:53.700
One the sides we have a headphone mic combo
jack along with three ports, two being full

00:02:53.700 --> 00:03:00.510
speed Thunderbolt 3 and the other USB-C but
for some reason only gen 1 meaning the speed

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:02.320
is only half of what it could be.

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:07.070
Now being MacBook fans we’re used to only
having USB-C ports, but it still is a bit

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:12.340
disappointing to see a $2000 laptop with less
ports than Apples equivalent that gets so

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:14.450
much hate for being a donglebook.

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:25.340
Our S940 has 512GB of SSD NVME SSD running
at a super fast 3341 MB/s Read and 1939 write

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:29.720
which is refreshing compared to other ultrabooks
that skimp on SSD’s.

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:33.910
So far this lenovo is getting sounding very
good overall, but this is where I have to

00:03:33.910 --> 00:03:38.960
get the few weak stops of this beautiful ultrabook,
and even though there’s not too much to

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:41.530
complain about these can really make or break
your decision.

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:52.200
First off, the webcam both looks poor and
sounds really muffled.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.120
Second is the battery life.

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:58.860
It makes sense that Lenovo could only fit
a 52watt hour battery in this ultra thin machine,

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:03.370
but pairing it to 500 nit 4K display results
in really poor battery life.

00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:08.950
Lenovo rates it at 7.5 hours of battery life
which in the real world is closer to 5 hours

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:14.820
with at usable display brightness levels.

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:17.889
This places it at the bottom of the market
for battery life if you want the gorgeous

00:04:17.889 --> 00:04:18.889
color accurate HDR display.

00:04:18.889 --> 00:04:22.719
Opting for the 1080P option will about double
your battery life, but that’s a big trade

00:04:22.719 --> 00:04:26.350
off since its not as bright and much lower
quality overall.

00:04:26.350 --> 00:04:30.949
Personally we wish they would have split it
right in the middle like Huawai or Apple with

00:04:30.949 --> 00:04:37.319
resolution in the middle of 1080P and 4K for
a detailed image and 10 hour battery life

00:04:37.319 --> 00:04:41.919
while maintaining 500 bit brightness, but
instead you have to choose from a top notch

00:04:41.919 --> 00:04:47.270
bright 4K display with poor battery life or
an average 1080P display with good battery

00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:49.560
life which is hard choice to make.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:52.020
The last downside is performance.

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:58.009
The spec sheet sounds very promising with
an 8th gen quad core 1.8Ghz processor that

00:04:58.009 --> 00:05:03.930
can boost up to 4.6Ghz but running a few tests
gave us disappointing results.

00:05:03.930 --> 00:05:09.580
The similarly priced 13” Macbook Pro scored
about 40% higher in Geekbench 4 and almost

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:14.909
60% higher in Cinebench R20 where all the
cores are maxed out, even though the MacBook

00:05:14.909 --> 00:05:17.710
is an i5 CPU not an i7.

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:25.960
Even comparing it to a $1299 base 1.4Ghz i5
MacBook Pro the Lenovo S940 falls really far

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:26.960
behind.

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:28.270
How is that possible you ask?

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:33.099
Well The CPU’s in these machines are all
rated at 15Watts, but the Lenovo is not letting

00:05:33.099 --> 00:05:37.700
the i7 run higher than that where the MacBooks
can continuously run at about 30watts which

00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:38.700
makes a huge difference in performance.

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:44.289
And yes, thats with all power saving features
turned off and with the S940 plugged in, while

00:05:44.289 --> 00:05:49.599
the Macbook Pro’s are on battery power without
having to find and change power options.

00:05:49.599 --> 00:05:54.150
Other windows laptops don’t limit the CPU
as much, but I can see why Lenovo is doing

00:05:54.150 --> 00:05:59.849
this giving the power draw of the bright 4K
display and the smaller battery capacity.

00:05:59.849 --> 00:06:05.150
Processor performance isn’t the only downside,
but the intel UHD Graphics 620 did struggle

00:06:05.150 --> 00:06:09.669
a bit with the 4K display causing occasional
UI stutters and also sometimes when playing

00:06:09.669 --> 00:06:11.669
back 4K Youtube videos.

00:06:11.669 --> 00:06:17.139
Of course this same GPU is used in most windows
equivalents but most of those have lower resolutions,

00:06:17.139 --> 00:06:21.669
and the 1080P version of the s940 shouldn’t
have these issues.

00:06:21.669 --> 00:06:26.400
On the Mac side, Apple pays more for intel
chips with IRIS graphics which provide more

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:30.830
than double the performance as you can see
in our Geekbench OpenCL test.

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:37.710
These downsides paired with a $2000 msrp make
the s940 a laptop that’s hard to recommend

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:40.030
even though we really like a lot about it.

00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:45.500
This is a really nice aluminum ultra thin
and light machine with only USB-C ports and

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:50.330
a gorgeous display at a premium price, Almost
like you’re buying a windows version of

00:06:50.330 --> 00:06:51.410
a Macbook.

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:54.580
We did a side by side comparison that you
can check out by using the card at the end

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:59.469
of this video, but the Macbook pro has much
better performance, 4 thunderbolt 3 ports,

00:06:59.469 --> 00:07:04.779
much better speakers and trackpad, a better
webcam and touch ID instead of windows hello

00:07:04.779 --> 00:07:09.790
and about double the battery life while having
an almost as sharp display with better color

00:07:09.790 --> 00:07:11.449
accuracy and similar brightness.

00:07:11.449 --> 00:07:16.129
You don’t have HDR for videos and the keyboard
is a way’s behind, but overall it provides

00:07:16.129 --> 00:07:17.749
a much better value for the price.

00:07:17.749 --> 00:07:18.749
And if you’re going for a lower priced model
Apple now sells the base model with almost

00:07:18.749 --> 00:07:19.749
identical CPU and GPU performance and the
same display, so even then the competition

00:07:19.749 --> 00:07:20.749
is strong.

00:07:20.749 --> 00:07:22.659
Now the main reason why we’re comparing
it to a MacBook is because Lenovo prioritized

00:07:22.659 --> 00:07:27.849
many things that Apple does and at a similar
price point, But of course not everyone wants

00:07:27.849 --> 00:07:33.270
a Mac and that’s where the new XPS 9580
or Razer Blade stealth come in, both having

00:07:33.270 --> 00:07:38.680
better port options, improved performance
and a lower regular price which make the S940

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:39.680
a hard sell.

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:44.240
But there is one reading factor, and that’s
the good discounts that lenovo offers on their

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:47.650
site, which we’ll link in the description.

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:54.639
Prices change but right now the $1800 model
is $360 off, which is only $60 cheaper than

00:07:54.639 --> 00:07:58.510
a similarly specced full price MacBook pro,
but at least at that price I can actually

00:07:58.510 --> 00:08:02.599
recommend it to one group of people, those
who do a lot of typing.

00:08:02.599 --> 00:08:08.330
For most even at that price a MacBook or XPS
is probably a better choice, but if you prioritize

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:13.370
design and want a thin and light windows laptop
that had a gorgeous screen to look at while

00:08:13.370 --> 00:08:19.930
you type away on the top notch keyboard for
up to 5 hours at a time the Lenovo S940 will

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:25.439
be a fantastic laptop for your needs, but
if you care about performance, battery life,

00:08:25.439 --> 00:08:29.139
ports and value more than design then you
should look elsewhere.

00:08:29.139 --> 00:08:34.520
Thanks for watching if you want to subscribe

